From 6630f1b49a5a03fad619699e944e40b07f5db483 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:05:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(privacy): Go back is a transition and a carried
 sign-in waits behind the wall

Deep audit 2026-11-09, findings A3 and A4 on this branch's entry notice
(js/live-content.js).

A3, "Privacy Go back leaves preserved document gate inert". Go back set
the wall's answers aside for good and relied on the browser throwing the
document away. A document the browser keeps and shows again (the
back/forward cache: Go back, then Forward), a step back that stays in the
same document, or a history with nothing behind the entry left a wall
with nothing to press. Leaving is a transition now:
- both answers are disabled only while the browser leaves;
- a restored document (a pageshow after a pagehide, or one that says
  persisted), a popstate or hashchange, or 1.5 s still on the page gives
  them back, with focus on Go back and never moved onto Agree;
- after a Go back that went nowhere, the next one leaves by the referrer
  or about:blank instead of asking history a second time;
- agreement recorded somewhere else (the Privacy Policy page, another
  tab, another McCluster host, the member's own account record) is read
  on pageshow, visibilitychange, window focus and storage, and takes the
  wall down where it stands, once. Nothing else does: release() has one
  caller, and that caller asks readAck() first.

A4, "Strict privacy entry remains exposed while handoff waits". A page
opened with #mcc_handoff= showed the whole site to a visitor who had not
agreed for up to ten seconds, on a fragment anyone can write. The wait is
behind the wall now: the page is concealed as the script runs in the
head, the dialog shows one status line and no answers, and the wait ends
in the question (refused, ten seconds without word of the sign-in, or no
reload four seconds after it) or in entry on the arriving member's own
record. The World takes the session where it stands (js/mnet.js cancels
mcc:handoff), so its record is read as soon as every listener has run
instead of four seconds later.

Tests. scripts/test/account-identity-gate.test.mjs gains six tests and
its harness learns persistent listeners, document events and a page that
is still loading; scripts/test/privacy-notice-policy.test.mjs pins what
may take the wall down. The existing handoff test asserted the defect
three times (shown() === false, "nothing while the handoff runs"). Those
three assertions now say what was meant, the question is not asked yet,
and what was missing, the page is concealed. No other existing assertion
changed.

Not changed: the two answers and their copy, the consent version, the
analytics gate, the policy page, js/tabbar.js, js/mnet.js.

